  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Raytheon has obligated $6.3B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Raytheon won 344 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $18.4M. Year-over-year obligations fell 41.0%. Historical obligations show variation by year: FY21 was $5.9B, FY22 was $7.4B, FY23 was $7.6B, FY24 was $7.8B, and FY25 was $10.7B. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is Raytheon’s largest market this fiscal year, accounting for $5.1B in obligations. Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing is the second market, with $801M obligated. Raytheon’s other notable markets include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $139M, Engineering Services at $126M, and Bare Printed Circuit Board Manufacturing at $54.6M. The FY2026 totals are partial, representing fiscal year to date obligations rather than full-year totals. Readers should treat FY2026 figures as incomplete for the full fiscal year, while the prior fiscal years listed are full-year totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Raytheon’s federal obligations changed year over year?",
        "body": "Raytheon’s obligations in FY2026 to date are $6.3B, down 41.0% year over year. Raytheon’s obligations rose from $5.9B in FY21 to $10.7B in FY25 before falling to $6.3B in FY26 (fiscal year to date). These numbers are presented as contract obligations, with FY2026 totals partial to the fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where does Raytheon spend its FY2026 federal obligations by market?",
        "body": "Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing accounted for $5.1B of Raytheon’s FY2026 obligations. Raytheon also recorded $801M in Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing, $139M in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences, and $126M in Engineering Services, with additional allocations across manufacturing, testing, and maintenance markets."
      }
    ]
  },
